WEBVTT

00:00:26.610 --> 00:00:30.290
Taeguk refers to the source of everything in the universe

00:00:30.290 --> 00:00:36.930
and the universal law in which everything continuously goes through cycles of creation and destruction.

00:00:36.930 --> 00:00:42.130
Pumse Taeguk symbolizes the root principle of universal philosophy

00:00:42.130 --> 00:00:47.410
and is constructed by applying the truth inherent in Taeguk's yin and yang principles.

00:00:48.290 --> 00:00:52.290
Taeguk Samjak stands for Yi of the eight trigrams

00:00:52.290 --> 00:00:57.330
and symbolizes fire which represents heat, brightness, and vitality.

00:00:57.330 --> 00:01:01.810
Taeguk Samjang is also the last stage of the initiatory training

00:01:01.810 --> 00:01:05.570
where you learn to move the center of your body in a stable manner,

00:01:05.570 --> 00:01:09.330
achieve harmonious movement of the body, and cultivate dexterity.

00:01:10.370 --> 00:01:13.730
We will now take a look at the Pumse of Taeguk Samjang.

00:02:04.350 --> 00:02:08.030
Taeguk Samjang consists of four key moves, namely

00:02:12.270 --> 00:02:21.870
These are the four key moves of Taeguk Samjang.

00:02:22.830 --> 00:02:27.230
We will now take a closer look at each of the key moves of Taeguk Samjang.

00:02:28.750 --> 00:02:34.910
Before explaining Sonal Anchigi, we will first look at ways to make the hand blade Sonnal.

00:02:36.510 --> 00:02:41.870
The hand blade used in the move extends from the wrist to the first joint of the little

00:02:41.950 --> 00:02:49.710
finger. First, open your hand. Place the four fingers from the index to the little finger together.

00:02:51.710 --> 00:02:57.230
Then, bend the tip of the thumb and place it on top of the first joint of the index finger

00:02:59.360 --> 00:03:08.140
and bend the tips a little inward. After making the hand blade as described,

00:03:09.020 --> 00:03:13.900
place the wrist of the thrusting arm at shoulder level and the supporting arm at

00:03:13.900 --> 00:03:25.330
the solar plexus level. Next, slightly twist your torso and perform the Sonnal Anchigi move

00:03:26.130 --> 00:03:32.740
by pulling both elbows towards your body. After completing the Sonnal Anchigi,

00:03:33.620 --> 00:03:41.580
place your supporting hand back at the wrist. The wrist of the striking hand should be straight

00:03:43.260 --> 00:03:46.220
and your hand blade should be raised near your neck level.

00:03:49.740 --> 00:03:56.540
Sonnal Pakkadmakki is also a technique that uses the hand blade in the same way as the previous

00:03:56.540 --> 00:04:05.040
move. You protect the body from the inside out and begin with two arms crossed in front of the

00:04:05.040 --> 00:04:12.400
chest. The defending arm and supporting arm should be placed on the outside and inside

00:04:12.400 --> 00:04:19.360
respectively when the arms are crossed. The tip of the hand of the defending arm should not be

00:04:19.360 --> 00:04:29.260
above the shoulder when defending and the elbow should face downward. Be careful not to let the

00:04:29.260 --> 00:04:35.100
wrist bend and the hand blade should not be outside the end of the line extending from the

00:04:35.100 --> 00:04:46.350
torso. When doing the Dwikubi posture, your feet should form a 90-degree angle and the

00:04:46.350 --> 00:04:54.610
direction of your knees and feet should be identical. The center of your body should be

00:04:54.610 --> 00:05:04.930
two-thirds towards the back. Move your left foot one step forward and stand low

00:05:04.930 --> 00:05:13.650
like you would for Juchumsogi. Double Jirugi is just what the name implies, two Jirugi moves

00:05:13.650 --> 00:05:21.090
in succession. Control your breath and quickly perform the Jirugi as if pulling your elbows

00:05:21.090 --> 00:05:30.240
to your waist. The force exerted and speed of your arms must be in balance. These are

00:05:30.240 --> 00:05:37.520
the four key moves of Taeguk Samjang. We will now look at the moves in succession connecting

00:05:37.520 --> 00:05:44.960
each move. The key moves of Taeguk Samjang first part consists of Wen Are Makki,

00:05:45.680 --> 00:05:56.000
Oren Apchagi, and Double Jirugi. Oren Are Makki, Wen Apchagi, and Double Jirugi.

00:05:56.320 --> 00:06:08.610
Oren Sonnal Anchigi, and Wen Sonnal Anchigi. When performing Oren Apchagi,

00:06:10.130 --> 00:06:19.300
bend your legs using momentum and first touch the ground with your front sole. Then quickly

00:06:19.300 --> 00:06:24.580
continue with Oren Jirugi while breathing once your rear sole touches the ground.

00:06:27.140 --> 00:06:30.580
The important thing is to quickly connect the Jirugi moves.

00:06:30.580 --> 00:06:36.740
You can achieve this by controlling your breath, removing unnecessary force, and making use of your

00:06:36.740 --> 00:06:44.510
spinning torso. When performing Doratdiki, push on the ground with your front foot,

00:06:44.510 --> 00:06:49.790
shifting your weight on the hind foot and naturally turn around and set your foot.

00:06:50.510 --> 00:06:57.260
When moving your center forward one step during Wen Apchagi and Oren Anchigi,

00:06:57.820 --> 00:07:04.700
move your left hand back and place one fist above the shoulder.

00:07:06.750 --> 00:07:12.670
Naturally straighten your right arm forward, set your right foot one step forward, then perform

00:07:12.670 --> 00:07:19.470
Oren Apchagi and Wen Sonnal Anchigi. Naturally straighten your right arm forward, then perform

00:07:19.470 --> 00:07:26.270
Anchigi, pulling your right elbow to your waist while doing this. Cautions for Taeguk Samjang

00:07:26.270 --> 00:07:32.910
First part, taking a closer look. When connecting Apchagi and Double Jirugi,

00:07:35.620 --> 00:07:40.340
the sole of the kicking foot should touch the ground first followed by the rear sole.

00:07:45.520 --> 00:07:52.640
When performing Double Jirugi, be careful not to exert unnecessary force. Use only muscular

00:07:52.640 --> 00:08:00.450
strength. We will now practice the moves of Taeguk Samjang. First part in succession

00:08:00.450 --> 00:08:22.060
while watching the video. The key moves of Taeguk Samjang. Second part consist of Wen Sonnal

00:08:22.060 --> 00:08:34.300
Pakatmaki, Oren Jirugi, Oren Sonnal Pakatmaki, Wen Jirugi, Oren Anmaki, and Wen Anmaki.

00:08:38.320 --> 00:08:43.360
During Sonnal Pakatmaki, the hand blade is used to defend by striking

00:08:43.440 --> 00:08:49.040
and is also intended to hold the opponent. Push on the ground with your right foot

00:08:49.040 --> 00:08:54.720
from the Oren Duikubi position and move your left foot forward about one and a half steps.

00:08:55.520 --> 00:09:01.740
The transition to Wen Apkubi. Shift your weight to your left foot.

00:09:03.420 --> 00:09:09.420
Raise the rear sole of your left foot and spin your heel using the sole as an axis.

00:09:10.860 --> 00:09:14.060
Then move and set your right foot to complete the Duikubi.

00:09:17.600 --> 00:09:24.080
When moving your center forward during Wen Apkubi and Oren Anmaki, you can perform the

00:09:24.080 --> 00:09:29.920
preparatory move by moving your left hand back and placing it about one fist above the shoulder,

00:09:31.040 --> 00:09:37.500
then naturally straightening your right arm forward. The right arm must naturally

00:09:37.500 --> 00:09:43.180
straighten forward and then the Oren Apkubi and Wen Anmaki can be performed by moving

00:09:43.180 --> 00:09:54.480
one step forward when doing this. Cautions for Taeguk Samjang second part, taking a closer look.

00:09:57.140 --> 00:10:00.660
Be careful not to perform Doradiki with your rear sole.

00:10:02.880 --> 00:10:07.280
When connecting to Jirugi after Duikubi Sonnal Pakatmaki,

00:10:07.280 --> 00:10:10.880
do not perform Jirugi after shifting your weight backwards.

00:10:13.700 --> 00:10:18.740
We will now practice the moves of Taeguk Samjang part 2 in succession while watching

00:10:18.740 --> 00:10:41.060
the video. The key moves of Taeguk Samjang third part consist of Wen Aremaki, Oren Apchagi,

00:10:41.060 --> 00:10:49.860
and Double Jirugi. Oren Aremaki and Wen Apchagi and Double Jirugi.

00:10:53.070 --> 00:10:58.350
We will now practice the moves of Taeguk Samjang third part in succession slowly while

00:10:58.350 --> 00:11:15.540
watching the video. The key moves of Taeguk Samjang fourth part consist of Wen Aremaki

00:11:15.540 --> 00:11:25.940
and Oren Jirugi. Oren Aremaki and Wen Jirugi. Wen Apchagi and Wen Aremaki and Oren Jirugi.

00:11:26.820 --> 00:11:36.370
Oren Apchagi and Oren Makki and Wen Jirugi. Control your breath after Aremaki

00:11:36.370 --> 00:11:39.810
and continue with Oren Jirugi by pulling the left below.

00:11:40.450 --> 00:11:46.290
I will try to explain the flow of the last moves of Taeguk Samjang for easier understanding.

00:11:46.290 --> 00:11:52.850
Fold your legs using the momentum right after Apchagi and at the same time prepare for Aremaki.

00:11:54.820 --> 00:11:59.620
You can then quickly connect the next Aremaki and Jirugi and add the shout.

00:12:03.380 --> 00:12:08.820
We will now practice the moves of Taeguk Samjang fourth part in succession slowly while

00:12:08.820 --> 00:12:30.140
watching the video. This concludes the training for Taeguk Samjang. We will take another look

00:12:30.220 --> 00:13:27.380
at all the moves and master Pumse. We have looked at the key moves of Taeguk Samjang

00:13:27.380 --> 00:13:32.980
and provided thorough explanations for each move and things to watch out for. Please

00:13:32.980 --> 00:13:38.580
focus on cultivating a harmonious movement of your body with dexterity while concentrating

00:13:38.580 --> 00:13:44.740
on the meaning of Taeguk Samjang symbolizing vitality and brightness. We will see you again

00:13:44.740 --> 00:13:48.020
in the Taeguk Samjang video. Thanks for watching!

